Z||000000||Dick McHaffie||03-29-2000||07:59 PM||||I know that there are a lot of Chevette and citation parts that will go into a fiero.<P>I have the 85GT V6 with manual trans and air, and it appears that I need a new radiator (in addition to the heater core I mentioned a few weeks ago).<P>I suppose that the radiator is something thats Fiero only.<P>Are there any interchangable radiators?<P>Also, Man! they sure made radiator cap difficult to get a grip on and place any pressure on it to get it removed.  Whats up with that?<P>...and I caught from a string a week or so ago that the thermostat is the highest spot in the cooling system.  Where is the thermostat?  It certainly doesn't jump out a me!<P>Thanks guys.  You are a big help.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Standard||03-29-2000||08:45 PM||||don't know about any interchangable radiatiors, but the thermostat is on the right side of the engine for the V6, left side of the duke.  just look for the silver cap that says "danger, pressurized" or something to that effect.<P>yeah, that radiator cap is a b!tch to get at...||||reg||1
Z||000002||BRIAN CORNELIUS||03-30-2000||12:11 AM||||To make the radiator cap easier to remove take a pliers and slightly bend the tow "tangs" on each side of the cap. Do not overdo it or it will not seal properly. Just enough to limit the friction a little. ||||reg||1
